                                                                <div class="dm-v4-questions-ai-title">Deal questions into balanced sets</div>
                                                                <div class="dm-v4-questions-ai-sub">The number of sets is capped by the rubric parameter with the fewest questions, because every set must cover every parameter without reusing a question.</div>
                                                            </div>
                                                        </div>
                                                        <button type="button" class="dm-v4-btn dm-v4-btn--primary dm-v4-btn--sm" id="dmV4CreateQuestionSetsBtn" title="Create balanced question sets for this channel"><i class="fa fa-clone"></i> Create sets</button>
                                                    </div>

                                                    @* The channel's explicit opt-in. Creating sets does not put them into use on its
                                                       own, so that a channel is never switched on before it has papers to deal. *@
                                                    <div class="dm-v4-questions-ai-banner">
                                                        <div class="dm-v4-questions-ai-banner__left">
                                                            <div>
                                                                <div class="dm-v4-questions-ai-title">Use these sets for interviews on this channel</div>
                                                                <div class="dm-v4-questions-ai-sub">Off means every candidate is asked the channel's questions in its standard order. On means each interview is locked to one set, so no two candidates in a batch answer the same paper. This also changes interview length to one question per rubric parameter. Interviews already locked to a set keep it if you switch this off.</div>
                                                            </div>
                                                        </div>
